   271|## Headless Export (Puppeteer)
   272|
   273|For automated, server-side, or CI rendering. Uses a headless Chrome browser to run the sketch.
   274|
   275|### export-frames.js (Node.js Script)
   276|
   277|See `scripts/export-frames.js` for the full implementation. Basic pattern:
   278|
   279|```javascript
   280|const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
   281|
   282|async function captureFrames(htmlPath, outputDir, options) {
   283|  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({
   284|    headless: true,
   285|    args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-setuid-sandbox']
   286|  });
   287|  const page = await browser.newPage();
   288|
   289|  await page.setViewport({
   290|    width: options.width || 1920,
   291|    height: options.height || 1080,
   292|    deviceScaleFactor: 1
   293|  });
   294|
   295|  await page.goto(`file://${path.resolve(htmlPath)}`, {
   296|    waitUntil: 'networkidle0'
   297|  });
   298|
   299|  // Wait for sketch to initialize
   300|  await page.waitForSelector('canvas');
   301|  await page.waitForTimeout(1000);
   302|
   303|  for (let i = 0; i < options.frames; i++) {
   304|    const canvas = await page.$('canvas');
   305|    await canvas.screenshot({
   306|      path: path.join(outputDir, `frame-${String(i).padStart(4, '0')}.png`)
   307|    });
   308|
   309|    // Advance one frame
   310|    await page.evaluate(() => { redraw(); });
   311|    await page.waitForTimeout(1000 / options.fps);
   312|  }
   313|
   314|  await browser.close();
   315|}
   316|```
   317|
   318|### render.sh (Full Pipeline)
   319|
   320|See `scripts/render.sh` for the complete render script. Pipeline:
   321|
   322|```
   323|1. Launch Puppeteer → open sketch HTML
   324|2. Capture N frames as PNG sequence
   325|3. Pipe to ffmpeg → encode H.264 MP4
   326|4. Optional: add audio track
   327|5. Clean up temp frames
   328|```
