   406|## CCapture.js — Deterministic Video Capture
   407|
   408|The built-in `saveFrames()` has limitations: small frame counts, memory issues, browser download blocking. CCapture.js solves all of these by hooking into the browser's timing functions to simulate constant time steps regardless of actual render speed.
   409|
   410|```html
   411|<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/ccapture.js-npmfixed/build/CCapture.all.min.js"></script>
   412|```
   413|
   414|### Basic Setup
   415|
   416|```javascript
   417|let capturer;
   418|let recording = false;
   419|
   420|function setup() {
   421|  createCanvas(1920, 1080);
   422|  pixelDensity(1);
   423|
   424|  capturer = new CCapture({
   425|    format: 'webm',       // 'webm', 'gif', 'png', 'jpg'
   426|    framerate: 30,
   427|    quality: 99,           // 0-100 for webm/jpg
   428|    // timeLimit: 10,      // auto-stop after N seconds
   429|    // motionBlurFrames: 4 // supersampled motion blur
   430|  });
   431|}
   432|
   433|function draw() {
   434|  // ... render frame ...
   435|
   436|  if (recording) {
   437|    capturer.capture(document.querySelector('canvas'));
   438|  }
   439|}
   440|
   441|function keyPressed() {
   442|  if (key === 'c') {
   443|    if (!recording) {
   444|      capturer.start();
   445|      recording = true;
   446|      console.log('Recording started');
   447|    } else {
   448|      capturer.stop();
   449|      capturer.save();  // triggers download
   450|      recording = false;
   451|      console.log('Recording saved');
   452|    }
   453|  }
   454|}
   455|```
   456|
   457|### Format Comparison
   458|
   459|| Format | Quality | Size | Browser Support |
   460||--------|---------|------|-----------------|
   461|| **WebM** | High | Medium | Chrome only |
   462|| **GIF** | 256 colors | Large | All (via gif.js worker) |
   463|| **PNG sequence** | Lossless | Very large (TAR) | All |
   464|| **JPEG sequence** | Lossy | Large (TAR) | All |
   465|
   466|### Important: Timing Hook
   467|
   468|CCapture.js overrides `Date.now()`, `setTimeout`, `requestAnimationFrame`, and `performance.now()`. This means:
   469|- `millis()` returns simulated time (perfect for recording)
   470|- `deltaTime` is constant (1000/framerate)
   471|- Complex sketches that take 500ms per frame still record at smooth 30fps
   472|- **Caveat**: Audio sync breaks (audio plays in real-time, not simulated time)
   473|
